From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:32:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] setProtectVoice: recompute the active voices

Protected voices are always mixed, but setProtectVoice did not mark the
active voice set dirty, so a newly protected voice stayed inactive (and an
unprotected one kept its place) until an unrelated play, stop, pause or
volume change recomputed the set.
---
 src/core/soloud_core_setters.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud_core_setters.cpp b/src/core/soloud_core_setters.cpp
index 718ff8e..1f4dc4f 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud_core_setters.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud_core_setters.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@ namespace SoLoud
 			{
 				mVoice[ch]->mFlags &= ~AudioSourceInstance::PROTECTED;
 			}
+			// Protection decides which voices are mixed.
+			mActiveVoiceDirty = true;
 		FOR_ALL_VOICES_POST
 	}
 
